Yes, tree shaking is an important optimization technique that can help reduce the size of the application bundle. Here are the steps to enable tree shaking in an Angular application:

1. In the `tsconfig.json` file, set the `"target"` property to `"es2015"`:


```json
{
 "compilerOptions": {
 "target": "es2015",
 ...
 }
}
```
2. In the `angular.json` file, set the `"optimization"` property to `true`:


```json
{
 "projects": {
 "my-project": {
 "architect": {
 "build": {
 "options": {
 "optimization": true,
 ...
 }
 }
 }
 }
 }
}
```
3. Ensure that all imports are static and don't use variables or dynamic expressions:


```typescript
// bad - dynamic import
const modulePath = './my-module';
import(modulePath).then((myModule) => {
 myModule.doSomething();
});

// good - static import
import { doSomething } from './my-module';
doSomething();
```
4. Avoid importing unused modules or functions:


```typescript
// bad - importing unused function
import { doSomething } from './my-module';
console.log('Hello world!');

// good - not importing unused function
console.log('Hello world!');
```
5. Use `@angular-devkit/build-optimizer` to further optimize the application. You can install it with the following command:


```
shellnpm install @angular-devkit/build-optimizer --save-dev
