If you want to put or update total availability based on its existence, you can use the `transactWrite` API to create a transaction that contains both a `put` and an `update` operation. The `put` operation will add a new item to the table with the specified primary key and availability count, and the `update` operation will update the availability count of an existing item with the same primary key.

Here's an example of how you can use `transactWrite` to put or update the total availability:


```javascript
async function putOrUpdateTotalAvailability(dynamoDbDocumentClient, date, specialization, appointmentType, sessionWindow, availability) {
 const pk = `TOTAL\_AVAILABILITY#${date}#${specialization}#${appointmentType}#${sessionWindow}`;
 const sk = 'TOTAL\_AVAILABILITY';

 const transactItems = [];

 // Check if the item already exists
 const getItemParams = {
 TableName: queryUtils.tableName(),
 Key: {
 PK: pk,
 SK: sk,
 },
 ProjectionExpression: 'AVAILABILITY',
 };

 const { Item: existingItem } = await dynamoDbDocumentClient.get(getItemParams).promise();

 if (existingItem) {
 // Item exists, update the availability count
 const updateParams = {
 TableName: queryUtils.tableName(),
 Key: {
 PK: pk,
 SK: sk,
 },
 UpdateExpression: 'SET AVAILABILITY = :availability',
 ConditionExpression: 'attribute\_exists(PK) and attribute\_exists(SK)', // Ensure the item exists before updating
 ExpressionAttributeValues: {
 ':availability': availability,
 },
 };

 transactItems.push({ Update: updateParams });
 } else {
 // Item doesn't exist, put a new item
 const putParams = {
 TableName: queryUtils.tableName(),
 Item: {
 PK: pk,
 SK: sk,
 AVAILABILITY: availability,
 },
 ConditionExpression: 'attribute\_not\_exists(PK) and attribute\_not\_exists(SK)', // Ensure the item doesn't exist before putting
 };

 transactItems.push({ Put: putParams });
 }

 // Perform the transaction
 const transactParams = {
 TransactItems: transactItems,
 };

 await dynamoDbDocumentClient.transactWrite(transactParams).promise();
}
```
